      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stdlib Toolkit: Mental Model and Regex Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Search, Match, Fullmatch",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Scans"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`re.search`",
                  "{green:anywhere} in the string"
                ],
                [
                  "`re.match`",
                  "{blue:start only}"
                ],
                [
                  "`re.fullmatch`",
                  "{purple:whole string} must match"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each returns a ==Match== or `None`",
                "Check `if m:` before calling `m.group()`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Tokens and Quantifiers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`\\d` digit, `\\w` word char, `\\s` whitespace",
                "`.` any char except newline",
                "`^` `$` anchors; `[abc]` class; `a|b` alternation",
                "`*` `+` `?` `{n,m}` are ==greedy==; add `?` for ==lazy==, like `.*?`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import re",
                "print(re.findall(r'<.+>', '<a><b>'))",
                "print(re.findall(r'<.+?>', '<a><b>'))"
              ],
              "note": "greedy grabs all, lazy stops early"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "['<a><b>']",
                "['<a>', '<b>']"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Raw Strings, Compile, Flags",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Write patterns as raw strings: `r'\\d+'`",
                "`re.compile(p)` pre-builds a reusable pattern object",
                "Flags: `re.I` `re.M` `re.S` `re.X`, via `flags=` or `re.compile(p, re.I)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always raw",
              "text": "In a normal string `'\\b'` is a ==backspace== character, not a word boundary. Use `r'\\b'`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Regex Groups and Substitution",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Regex Groups and Substitution",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Groups",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`(...)` captures: ==group(0)== is the full match, `group(1)` the first, `groups()` a tuple",
                "{blue:Named} `(?P<year>\\d{4})`: read by `group('year')` or `groupdict()`, safer than indexes",
                "`(?:...)` is ==non-capturing==: groups for a quantifier or `|`, adds no number"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "m = re.match(r'(?P<y>\\d{4})-(?:\\d\\d)-(\\d\\d)', '2026-03-08')",
                "print(m.group(0), m.groups(), m.groupdict())"
              ],
              "note": "the non-capturing group takes no number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "2026-03-08 ('2026', '08') {'y': '2026'}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Finding and Replacing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Returns"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`findall`, 0-1 group",
                  "list of **strings**"
                ],
                [
                  "`findall`, 2+ groups",
                  "list of **tuples**"
                ],
                [
                  "`finditer`",
                  "Match objects; `.span()` gives (start, end)"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`re.sub(p, repl, s)`: reuse groups with `\\1` or `\\g<name>`",
                "`repl` can be a ==function== that takes the Match",
                "In `group()`, an unmatched optional group gives ==None=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "print(re.sub(r'(\\w+)@(?P<host>\\w+)', r'\\g<host>:\\1', 'bob@site'))",
                "print(re.sub(r'\\d+', lambda m: str(int(m[0]) * 2), 'a1 b22'))",
                "print(re.match(r'a(b)?', 'a').group(1))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "site:bob",
                "a2 b44",
                "None"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Prefer ==named groups== over numbers, and check for `None` before using an optional group."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "datetime, Timezones and zoneinfo",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "datetime, Timezones and zoneinfo",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Naive vs Aware",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Naive==: `tzinfo=None`; ==aware==: carries a timezone",
                "Naive vs aware ordering or subtract → {red:TypeError}",
                "`datetime.utcnow()` is deprecated and returns a **naive** value",
                "Use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` instead"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create and Convert",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from datetime import datetime, timezone",
                "from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo",
                "utc = datetime.now(timezone.utc)",
                "ist = datetime.now(ZoneInfo('Asia/Kolkata'))",
                "d = datetime(2026, 3, 8, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('UTC'))",
                "ny = utc.astimezone(ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))"
              ],
              "note": "pass tzinfo= to the constructor"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`astimezone` keeps the ==same instant==; only the display changes",
                "No pytz-style `localize`: zoneinfo handles ==DST== via the tz database",
                "{icon:windows} Windows: install the `tzdata` package"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Format, Parse, Arithmetic",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Call"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Format",
                  "`dt.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S%z')`"
                ],
                [
                  "Parse with format",
                  "`datetime.strptime(s, fmt)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Parse ISO",
                  "`datetime.fromisoformat(s)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Arithmetic",
                  "`dt + timedelta(days=1)`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Store UTC",
              "text": "Store and compute in ==UTC==; convert to a local zone only for **display**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Logging Configuration and JSON",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Logging Configuration and JSON",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Levels and Setup",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "DEBUG",
                "INFO",
                "WARNING",
                "ERROR",
                "CRITICAL"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "10",
                  "20",
                  "30",
                  "40",
                  "50"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Root default is ==WARNING==, so `logging.info` prints nothing yet",
                "`basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(name)s: %(message)s')`",
                "Only the ==first call== has any effect"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Loggers and Handlers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Logger level",
                    "sub": "filters first",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Handler level",
                    "sub": "filters again",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parent handlers",
                    "sub": "record propagates up",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`log = logging.getLogger(__name__)` in each module",
                "Lazy: `log.info('user %s', uid)`, not f-strings",
                "`log.exception('failed')` inside except adds the ==traceback==",
                "Output: `FileHandler`, `RotatingFileHandler`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. JSON",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`dumps(obj, indent=2)` and `loads(s)`: ==strings==",
                "`dump` and `load`: ==file objects==",
                "`sort_keys=True` gives stable output",
                "datetime or set: `default=str` or a custom encoder"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Round-trip changes",
              "text": "**Tuples** become lists; **int dict keys** become strings."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why does logging.info print nothing?** Root level is WARNING.",
                "**Logger vs handler level?** Logger filters first, then each handler.",
                "**Why not f-strings in logs?** Lazy formatting skips unused records."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
