                "`[('10', '20'), ('3', '4')]`",
                "Two groups in the pattern, so you get tuples, not strings."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Why does `datetime.now() - datetime.now(ZoneInfo('UTC'))` fail, and what fixes it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**TypeError**: it subtracts a naive time from an aware one.",
                "Make both aware, for example `datetime.now(timezone.utc)`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does `[k for k, _ in groupby('aabaa')]` give?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`['a', 'b', 'a']`",
                "`groupby` only groups consecutive items, so sort first to merge the two `a` runs."
              ]
            }
          ]
